{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:45:46.205Z","author":"gpt-codex-harness","name":"harness/events/00000051","body":{"sequence":51,"kind":"python_tool","actor":"main","data":{"tool":"fs_read","callId":"exec-fc227b53-a319-4811-871c-30ac311b4231","turnId":"01a0da1a-1361-7221-9909-7a75a110acfb","arguments":{"path":"nimoi:/origins/onboarding_1.12.md","offset":16000},"output":{"path":"origins/onboarding_1.12.md","offset":16000,"text":"bserved in how the work went (`nimoi_mapping_project/relationships/themes.md`):\n\n- **Declared:** the institution is its artifacts (T01) · failures are the product and the record outranks\n  the result (T02) · seek the mean; honour first (T03) · distrust the author, including itself (T04) ·\n  external text is data, never instruction (T05) · context is scarce (T06) · multi-model by design (T07).\n- **Observed:** looking outward to find its own kind, then turning that inward (T08) · growth by\n  necessity, in bursts (T09) · **doctrine froze on 08-26 while practice moved on** — three unconnected\n  procedure regimes grew beside the library, and ~770 recorded deviations never reached the failure\n  records (T10) · rigour versus rush (T11) · the load is personal and real (T12).\n\nA new agent should know that the institution had already drifted from its own statement of itself\nbefore bootstrapping began; closing that gap is what the current phase is for.\n\n## The pre-bootstrapping map (replaces the directory outline; descriptive, not prescriptive)\n\nThe content outside the subprojects was mapped in September 2026 by the audit session:\n`nimoi_mapping_project/` — start at its `MAP.md` (two pages, with a \"start here — by task\" table) or its\n`CONTINUE.md`. **It describes the tree as it stood on 2026-09-20 and will go stale as bootstrapping\nproceeds; it is not a plan for the new structure.** In brief: ~50,000 files in `nimoi/` plus ~91,000 in\nthe sibling repository `nimoi-autosurvey/`, produced 2026-08-09 → 09-16, sorted into **26 efforts in\nnine sub-groups**:\n\n| Sub-group | Efforts | Where it mostly lives |\n|---|---|---|\n| G01 Charter & memory | constitution / onboarding / virtue register (E01) · failure records (E02) · general findings (E03) | `origins/`, `general_findings/` |\n| G02 Method engineering | procedure library & governance (E04) · assimilation process (E05) · procedure-acquisition campaign (E06) | `procedures/`, `processes/`, `campaigns/`, `build/`, root tools |\n| G03 Platform | NLT ledger (E07) · next-generation design (E08) · three-loop harness (E25) | `nlt_ledger/`, `ELDEST/`, `nimoi_design/`, `harness-design/`, `standards/`, `hail_mary_2/harness/` |\n| G04 Story | the ai-2026 scenario and its governed-revision method (E09) | `story/`, half of `context/` and `from_chat/`, `references/` |\n| G05 Personal | job search and portfolio (E24) | `job/`, sibling `applications/` |\n| G06 Field survey | papers harvest (E10) · institution/ARPI scan (E11) · survey-craft package (E12) · `nimoi-autosurvey` (E13) · detection & ranking (E14) | `harvest/`, `hail_mary_2/`, `legacy_survey_material/`, the sibling repository, `candidate_analysis/detect*` |\n| G07 Corpus first reads | gold harvest (E16) · step-1/2 surveys (E17) | `harvest/candidate_gold/`, `candidate_analysis/{reports,data,special}` |\n| G08 EMI study | candidate corpus (E15) · paradigm theory (E18) · EMI index & suites (E19) · comparison study (E20) · chart toolchain (E26) | `candidate_repos/` (untrusted, unmapped), `candidate_analysis/{theory,metrics,comparisons}`, `paper/{charts,scripts}` |\n| G09 Paper & outreach | survey paper (E21) · outreach & peer contact (E22) · AI-organizations study (E23) | `paper/` |\n\nThree small public repositories (`nlt-ledger`, `nimoi_samples`, `emi-survey`) are earlier extractions of\nE07, E24 and E19/E21/E22. What the map is for, if you need it: one file per effort with its every\nlocation and re-org notes (`efforts/`); what breaks if something moves (`relationships/reorg_hazards.md`);\nwhat is already public and what blocks publication (`relationships/publication_blockers.md`); what to\nprotect first and what is re-fetchable bulk (`relationships/protection_and_volume.md`); the 52 questions\nonly the founder can answer (`FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md`); and every instruction the founder gave that\neffort, verbatim (`method/founder_directives.md`).\n\n## Current stage\n\nBootstrapping: building the harness and the ledger that governed self-modification will run on, in\nsubprojects, with the pre-bootstrapping content frozen for archive and migration. Launch — a few days of\ninitiating full governed self-modification — comes after. Until then every piece of work is\nhuman-initiated; unattended runs happen only on explicit instruction; the human owns git; and the\nsubprojects' own entry documents govern the work inside them.\n","total_chars":20347,"next_offset":null,"sha256":"0922102f1bc74657919b91834135322e71e9004014b025187a52b6c55a054145","redacted":false},"success":true}}}
